# Facts for the sync error observation gate (_get_errors, sync.py:44-75).
# sync.state: compile_status stripped to its first pipe-segment (idle | idle-failed | compiling | …).
# sync.hasCsErrors: True when 'error CS' appears in the corroborated errors string.
# sync.hasErrors: True when the corroborated errors string is non-empty.
# sync.isWarnOnly: True when errors contain '[warn:' but NOT 'error CS'.
# sync.diagnosticIssue: True when _verdict starts with FAIL:/BUILD-FAILED-WEDGE, or reload_failed,
#   or compile/sync are actively busy (iscompiling, cn_active, is_really_compiling, reload in progress).
# sync.hasStaleDlls: True when any parsed DLL token has status == 'stale'.
# Outputs: errors/failedNoDetails/unknown/unknownState → non-empty blocking verdicts;
#          verdict → delegated from _verdict(); failStaleDll → FAIL:stale-dll; clean → '' (ok).
CONTRACT unitymcp.syncerrors
COVERAGE declared-scope
MODULE syncerrors_facts
FACT sync.state enum=idle,idleFailed,other open
FACT sync.hasCsErrors bool
FACT sync.hasErrors bool
FACT sync.isWarnOnly bool
FACT sync.diagnosticIssue bool
FACT sync.hasStaleDlls bool
INPUT syncErrors sync.state sync.hasCsErrors sync.hasErrors sync.isWarnOnly sync.diagnosticIssue sync.hasStaleDlls
